rusts cable tension more than politicians.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep every skybridge safe and prevent another collapse like the one that killed her apprentice.","goal":"Secure funding and legal cover to inspect all Cartel-managed bridges.","flaw":"Rigid adherence to Warden protocol makes her slow to act on unofficial evidence.","internal_conflict":"She believes in the Wardens' neutrality but sees that neutrality is helping the Cartel.","external_conflict":"Rising tolls starve her crews of materials while the Toll War limits her inspection authority.","arc":"Starts as a by-the-book engineer who dismisses rumors. When Isolde brings her charts showing a sabotaged cable pattern matching her apprentice's collapse, she breaks protocol and orders an unsanctioned inspection. She ends as an outspoken Warden willing to challenge her own council.","personality_traits":["blunt","loyal","practical","weary"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Weaves and repairs skybridge cable with unmatched strength.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Fault Reading","description":"Diagnoses sabotage in cable fibers by touch and sound.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_reed","name":"Tobin Reed","role":"supporting","description":"A wiry young miller from The Hollow, early twenties, with flour-dusted hair and a quick grin. He leads the youth of the Hollow Circle and has learned to count grain tallies faster than any Cartel clerk.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect his village from starvation caused by the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Smuggle an untaxed grain shipment across Mistral Docks to prove the levy is unenforceable.","flaw":"Reckless impulsiveness leads him to act before planning.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between the Circle's quiet patience and his hunger for dramatic action.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy leaves his 