ed brocade. He rose from dockside clerk to negotiator of shipping lanes and is the late diplomat's chief opponent in the toll talks.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's toll charter permanently and protect the fortune he built from nothing.","goal":"Steer the investigation toward a scapegoat while destroying the diplomat's letters about unpaid wind-debts.","flaw":"Greed that makes him take reckless risks to avoid any loss.","internal_conflict":"He despises the privileged class he serves yet craves their acceptance.","external_conflict":"Isolde's inquiry threatens to expose the Cartel's falsified wind-debt ledgers during the Toll War.","arc":"Corvin starts confident that influence can bury any inquiry. When he pays to have the diplomat's letters stolen, the attempt leaves a trail Isolde follows. Cornered at the unmasking, he is exposed and loses the acceptance he craved, ending a ruined man.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","insecure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Persuades and bargains his way past officials and rivals.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","name":"Tamsin Reeve","description":"A wiry young dockhand at Mistral Docks, Tamsin has weathered skin, cropped red hair and a patched coat. She works the carnival lantern-barges wearing a cheap paper bird mask and saw a figure leave the palazzo moments before the body was found.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To clear the wind-debt that is crushing her family.","goal":"Sell what she saw safely, without being punished by her Cartel employers.","flaw":"Fear of authority makes her evasive and prone to lying.","internal_conflict":"She wants the debt cleared but is ashamed of profiting from a death.","external_conflict":"Corvin's agents watch the docks and threaten her livelihood if she talks.","arc":"Tamsin begins silent and terrified of the Cartel. After Isolde dismisses her at first, a threat to her brother pushes her to testify publicly at the unmasking. She ends braver and freed from her debt by the Wardens' protection.","personality_traits":["quick","wary","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Dock Sense","description":"Knows every barge, rope and face moving through the port.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_aldric_voss","name":"Aldric Voss","description":"A stern Bridge Warden captain from Emberroost, broad-shouldered and soot-marked, who wears a bronze ram mask. He is the diplomat's old ally in demanding lower tolls and was the last to speak with him.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe and funded despite Cartel tolls.","goal":"Protect the Wardens' reputation and avoid being named a suspect.","flaw":"Stubborn secrecy: he hides inconvenient facts to protect his institution.","internal_conflict":"His loyalty to the Wardens conflicts with his duty to the truth about his friend's death.","external_conflict":"As the last person seen with the diplomat, he is the Cartel's favoured scapegoat in the Toll War.","arc":"Aldric starts by concealing a private argument he had with the diplomat. When Corvin's scapegoating nearly hangs him, he admits the quarrel to Isolde. He ends by trusting the truth over institutional pride.","personality_traits":["loyal","gruff","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bridge Engineering","description":"Reads cable and cloudstone damage to tell how a crossing was used.","category":"technological"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_adversary","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vanterre","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_halsey","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Vanterre investigates Corvin Halsey, whose Cartel interests depend on the case ending without scrutiny of the wind-debt ledgers."},{"id":"rel_corvin_tamsin_threat","