ed brocade. He rose from dockside clerk to negotiator of shipping lanes and is the late diplomat's chief opponent in the toll talks.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's toll charter permanently and protect the fortune he built from nothing.","goal":"Steer the investigation toward a scapegoat while destroying the diplomat's letters about unpaid wind-debts.","flaw":"Greed that makes him take reckless risks to avoid any loss.","internal_conflict":"He despises the privileged class he serves yet craves their acceptance.","external_conflict":"Isolde's inquiry threatens to expose the Cartel's falsified wind-debt ledgers during the Toll War.","arc":"Corvin starts confident that influence can bury any inquiry. When he pays to have the diplomat's letters stolen, the attempt leaves a trail Isolde follows. Cornered at the unmasking, he is exposed and loses the acceptance he craved, ending a ruined man.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","insecure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Persuades and bargains his way past officials and rivals.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_reeve","name":"Tamsin Reeve","description":"A wiry young dockhand at Mistral Docks, Tamsin has weathered skin, cropped red hair and a patched coat. She works the carnival lantern-barges wearing a cheap paper bird mask and saw a figure leave the palazzo moments before the body was found.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To clear the wind-debt that is crushing her family.","goal":"Sell what she saw safely, without being punished by her Cartel employers.","flaw":"Fear of authority makes her evasive and prone to lying.","internal_conflict":"She wants the debt cleared but is ashamed of profiting from a death.","external_conflict":"Corvin's agents watch the docks and threaten her livelihood if she talks.","arc":"Ta