ixties with a hawk-like face and keys at her belt. She keeps the wards in permanent lamplessness and enforces strict order. She was once a Bridge Warden's daughter and believes in keeping fragile things bound by rules.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To protect the patients and the asylum's secret from outside scrutiny that she believes would destroy both.","goal":"Drive Dr. Voss away, or keep his findings from ever leaving the asylum.","flaw":"Controlling pride that treats every doubt as betrayal.","internal_conflict":"She suspects her strict regime feeds the dream she claims to be containing.","external_conflict":"Voss's investigation threatens the secret she has guarded, and the Wind-debt owed for the asylum's supplies binds her to suppliers who want answers.","arc":"Begins as a gatekeeper who hides the dream's origin behind discipline. When Voss shows her that the dream deepens after each lights-out she enforces, she is forced to choose between her rules and her patients. She unlocks the records ward and turns her authority to helping Voss, ending as a reluctant ally who admits her control was fear.","personality_traits":["severe","loyal","secretive","disciplined"],"abilities":[{"name":"Institutional Authority","description":"Commands staff absolutely and controls access to every ward.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_wren","name":"Tobias Wren","description":"A gaunt twenty-six-year-old former Drift Cartel deckhand who was committed after screaming about a staircase descending into a sky with no end. He is the first patient to dream the shared dream, and he draws it obsessively with charcoal on any scrap he can find.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To make someone finally believe the dream is real so he is no longer alone in it.","goal":"Get his drawings of the dream into Voss's hands before the next lights-out.","flaw":"Paranoia that makes him hide the very evidence he needs others to see.","internal_conflict":"He cannot tell whether he is remembering the dream or being written into it.","external_conflict":"Orderlies confiscate his drawings, and he owes the Cartel a debt that his family still pays.","arc":"Starts as a terrified patient who hoards and hides his drawings. After Voss returns a confiscated sketch and listens without judging, Tobias trusts him enough to hand over the full set. He ends as the key witness who finally speaks plainly about the dream.","personality_traits":["fearful","creative","intense"],"abilities":[{"name":"Dream Sketching","description":"Draws precise and unsettling images of the shared dream.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_ines_calder","name":"Ines Calder","description":"A soft-spoken night nurse in her thirties, once a Hollow Circle miller's daughter. She is pale from long night shifts and moves silently through the dark wards. She is the only staff member who has begun to dream the dream herself.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To spare the patients' suffering and stop the dream spreading to her own family.","goal":"Secretly give Voss access to the night records without being caught by Matron Hale.","flaw":"Conflict avoidance that makes her silent when she should speak.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between loyalty to Hale, who gave her work, and the conscience that urges her to expose what she has seen.","external_conflict":"Hale watches the night staff closely, and Ines's family farm owes the asylum a wind-debt that Hale holds over her.","arc":"Begins as a silent witness who looks away from what she sees at night. After finding her own name in Tobias's drawings, she risks her post to pass Voss the night ledger. She ends as the one who speaks up, ready to bear Hale's anger.","personality_traits":["gentle","anxious","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Night Rounds Knowledge","description":"Knows every hidden corridor and the schedule of the dark wards.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_voss_hale_conflict","source_character_id":"chr_elias_voss","target_character_id":"chr_margarethe_hale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Dr. Elias Voss and Matron Margarethe Hale clash over control of the asylum's records and wards; her obstruction directly fuels his suspicion."},{"id":"rel_hale_voss_obstruct","source_character_id":"chr_margarethe_hale","target_character_id":"chr_elias_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Matron Margarethe Hale sees Dr. Elias Voss as a threat to the asylum's secret and works to isolate him from patients and staff."},{"id":"rel_voss_wren_patient","source_character_id":"chr_elias_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Dr. Elias Voss treats Tobias Wren and becomes the first person to take his drawings seriously, drawing Voss deeper into the dream."},{"id":"rel_calder_voss_ally","source_character_id":"chr_ines_calder","target_character_id":"chr_elias_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ines Calder secretly aids Dr. Elias Voss with night records, betraying Matron Hale's trust to do so."},{"id":"rel_hale_calder_control","source_character_id":"chr_margarethe_hale","target_character_id":"chr_ines_calder","relationship_type":"employer","description":"Matron Margarethe Hale holds Ines Calder's livelihood and family wind-debt over her, keeping the nurse silent and compliant."}]}
