A heavy-set merchant prince of the Drift Cartel in his fifties, Corvane holds the shipping contracts of Mistral Docks and seeks a monopoly over the skybridge routes. He wears a black frock coat with a gold chain of office and keeps his white beard oiled. He rose by buying the debts of rivals and neighbours.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"Secure total control of inter-isle transit so that no one can cross a bridge without paying him.","goal":"Move the stolen locomotive to the terminus and use it to seize the cloudstone cable stores and force the Toll War to his terms.","flaw":"Contempt for his underlings that blinds him to their betrayals.","internal_conflict":"He cannot decide whether he wants power for security or merely to prove that he is not the dockhand's son he once was.","external_conflict":"The Bridge Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist his tolls and levies, and the marshal and con artist are racing to stop him.","arc":"Corvane begins as a confident monopolist who trusts his hired hands. When Silas turns the locomotive's brake against him at the terminus, his plan collapses publicly. He ends stripped of his charter and forced to face the debtors he once crushed.","personality_traits":["calculating","imperious","patient","vindictive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Brokerage","description":"Buys and weaponises wind-debts to bind people to his will.","category":"social"},{"name":"Cartel Network","description":"Commands shipping crews, informants and hired gunmen.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_odalys_brant","name":"Odalys Brant","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered Hollow Circle miller in her late twenties, Odalys runs the windmill that supplies grain for the locomotive's route. She has flour-dusted forearms, close-cropped hair and a calm voice. She quietly feeds both sides because she believes that hunger knows no faction.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"Protect her community from the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Hide enough grain stores to feed the Hollow through the season and recruit the marshal to stop the levy.","flaw":"Reluctance to take sides, which leaves her passive until the danger is on her doorstep.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between the Circle's quiet neutrality and her wish to fight the baron openly.","external_conflict":"Baron Corvane's agents demand her grain while the Cartel threatens to stop her wind-debt repayments.","arc":"Odalys starts as a neutral miller who feeds anyone who asks. When Cartel agents try to seize her grain during the chase, she hides the marshal and con artist in her mill and rallies the Circle to block the tracks. She ends as an active leader of the Hollow's resistance.","personality_traits":["patient","practical","warm","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Weather Sense","description":"Predicts the wind shifts that affect the drift and the locomotive's route.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Community Organising","description":"Mobilises farmers and millers on short notice.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ines_calder","name":"Ines Calder","role":"supporting","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy, Ines is slight, bespectacled and perpetually ink-smudged. She charts the shifting skybridge network and discovers that the baron's route requires a bridge that is about to fail.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"Prove that careful mapping can save lives and earn a place among the senior cartographers.","goal":"Warn the marshal about the failing span and chart a safe route for the locomotive.","flaw":"Timid perfectionism that makes her withhold findings until she is certain.","internal_conflict":"She fears being wrong more than she fears the disaster her silence might cause.","external_conflict":"The Academy's senior staff dismiss her survey while Cartel agents try to buy her charts.","arc":"Ines starts as a hesitant junior who keeps her survey hidden. When she realises that the baron's route crosses a failing span, she sends an uncertain warning to Marshal Veil and then personally guides the locomotive to a safe bridge. She ends as a confident chartmaster who acts on imperfect data.","personality_traits":["meticulous","anxious","curious","brave when cornered"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Maps and predicts the drift of the skybridge network.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_silas_pursuit","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veil","target_character_id":"chr_silas_quill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Marshal Mara Veil hunts Silas Quill as the thief of the locomotive, and her rigid law clashes with his lies, but they must work together to stop Baron Corvane."},{"id":"rel_silas_corvane_debt","source_character_id":"chr_silas_quill","target_character_id":"chr_baron_corvane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Silas Quill is bound to Baron Corvane by a wind-debt that forced him to steal the locomotive, and Corvane threatens Silas's sister's family to keep him obedient."},{"id":"rel_corvane_mara_opposition","source_character_id":"chr_baron_corvane","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veil","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Baron Corvane sees Marshal Mara Veil as the Bridge Wardens' enforcer who blocks his monopoly, and he sends hired guns to stop her."},{"id":"rel_odalys_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_brant","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veil","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Odalys Brant shelters Marshal Mara Veil in the Hollow and pushes her to protect the grain farmers from Baron Corvane's levy."},{"id":"rel_ines_mara_informant","source_character_id":"chr_ines_calder","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veil","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ines Calder sends Marshal Mara Veil survey warnings about the failing span, and Mara's trust gives the timid 