{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_tobias_varn","name":"Commander Tobias Varn","role":"protagonist","description":"A lean, weathered officer of about forty who commands the Mistral Docks fleet squadron. He has a close-cropped grey beard, a rope-scarred left palm, and a plain blue coat with no ornament. He left the family holding on the Hollow as a young man and rose through the ranks on discipline alone. He has not spoken to his younger brother Idris in fifteen years, since their father's death and a quarrel over the grain debts that followed.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","personality_traits":["stoic","disciplined","dutiful","guarded","precise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fleet Tactics","description":"Reads wind currents and skybridge geometry to position sail-ships so they hold the best lane.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Steady Command","description":"His calm voice keeps crews orderly under pressure and in storms.","category":"social"}],"motivation":"To prove that duty and order can hold the archipelago together, as he swore to his dying father.","goal":"Break the enemy blockade of the skybridge lanes and bring the war to an end with the fewest ships lost.","flaw":"He buries every feeling under duty and cannot say what he needs from others.","internal_conflict":"His loyalty to the fleet and its Cartel masters pulls against his guilt over abandoning his brother.","external_conflict":"He must defeat an admiral who turns out to be Idris, while the Toll War makes the Cartel's cause less just each season.","arc":"Starts as a man who hides behind orders and has never answered Idris's last letter. When a captured dispatch reveals that the enemy admiral is Idris, he must choose between sinking the flagship at Silverspine's skybridge chokepoint and offering terms. He chooses to meet Idris under truce and admits his fault openly. He ends as a commander who puts honesty ahead of rank."},{"id":"chr_idris_varn","name":"Admiral Idris Varn","role":"antagonist","description":"Tobias's younger brother, about thirty-six, broad-shouldered and sunburnt, with a clipped, formal way of speaking that echoes his brother's. He stayed among the Hollow farmers after their father died and watched the Cartel levy strip the harvest. He now commands the Hollow Circle's fleet of converted grain-barges, which he has drilled into a disciplined war fleet.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","personality_traits":["resolute","proud","principled","austere","resentful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Improvised Fleet Craft","description":"Turns slow grain-barges into a coordinated battle line using wind-drift and shielded signal lamps.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Rallying Presence","description":"Holds together farmers and millers who have little military training.","category":"social"}],"motivation":"To end the Cartel's grain levy so the Hollow's people are never starved for tolls again.","goal":"Force the Cartel to repeal the Grain Levy by closing its shipping lanes.","flaw":"He carries a grudge against Tobias and will not accept that his brother may have changed.","internal_conflict":"He is fighting for the Hollow's survival but is coming to see that the war is destroying what he wants to protect.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy puts him in direct conflict with the Drift Cartel, and the fleet that blocks him is led by his own brother.","arc":"Starts as a hardened admiral who sees Tobias only as a Cartel instrument. After a convoy of Hollow barges is lost to a wind-debt collapse he sees that the blockade is starving the people he swore to protect, and Tobias's offer of a truce arrives at that moment. He accepts the meeting, ends as a leader willing to bargain, and gives up the grudge."},{"id":"chr_maren_solt","name":"Lieutenant Maren Solt","role":"supporting","description":"A sharp-eyed navigator of about twenty-eight with ink-stained fingers and a cartographer's habit of sketching every course. She trained at Silverspine Academy before joining Tobias's flagship, and serves as his flag lieutenant and confidant.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","personality_traits":["curious","candid","observant","principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts shifting skybridge routes and predicts where crossings will open or close.","category":"mental"}],"motivation":"To keep the skybridge network safe for everyone, whatever flag the ships fly.","goal":"Make sure the war does not damage the bridges, and persuade Tobias to spare them in battle.","flaw":"She speaks bluntly and often undermines her commander's authority in front of the crew.","internal_conflict":"Her Warden oath to protect the bridges conflicts with her sworn duty to a Cartel-funded fleet.","external_conflict":"The Toll War sets Wardens against Cartel merchants, which puts her between her own faction and her commander.","arc":"Starts as an officer who voices objections loudly and gets ignored. When Tobias hesitates over firing near a loaded skybridge she delivers her case privately, with charts, instead of in front of the crew. He listens and re-routes the squadron. She ends as a trusted adviser who knows when and how to speak."}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_varn_brothers_estranged","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_varn","target_character_id":"chr_idris_varn","relationship_type":"estranged sibling","description":"Tobias Varn and Idris Varn are brothers who split over their father's grain debts and have not spoken in fifteen years. Their shared past and opposed fleets drive the central conflict."},{"id":"rel_idris_tobias_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_idris_varn","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_varn","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Idris Varn sees Tobias Varn as the Cartel's loyal instrument and the brother who abandoned the Hollow, which hardens his resolve in battle."},{"id":"rel_maren_tobias_adviser","source_character_id":"chr_maren_solt","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_varn","relationship_type":"mentee","description":"Maren Solt serves as flag lieutenant to Tobias Varn, pushing him to protect the skybridges and to face his brother, which pressures his rigid sense of duty."}]}
