sive of anyone he considers small or powerless.","internal_conflict":"He privately resents the Cartel's cruelty but suppresses that doubt to protect his ambition.","external_conflict":"The Hollow Circle resists the Grain Levy, and the strange events caused by Pip threaten his tallies and his reputation.","arc":"Orrin begins as a confident collector who sees the Hollow as a ledger line. When he is confused by Pip's repeated appearances in yesterday during the Grain Levy standoff, he discovers a child outwitting his schedule and is forced to confront the human cost of his tallies. He ends by quietly reporting a reduced levy, trading ambition for conscience.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","secretly conflicted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Mind","description":"Can recall every figure in a ledger after one reading.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Persuades and pressures with polished negotiation.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_juniper_quill","name":"Juniper Quill","role":"supporting","description":"A young cartographer-apprentice at Silverspine Academy with ink-stained fingers, round spectacles, and a habit of muttering coordinates. She charts skybridges and becomes intrigued by anomalies in yesterday's maps.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that the shifting skybridge network follows a hidden pattern.","goal":"To map the anomaly of the yesterday door and publish it at the Academy.","flaw":"Overly rigid; she distrusts anything that cannot be measured.","internal_conflict":"Her love of order clashes with her growing wonder at something that defies measurement.","external_conflict":"The Toll War strains the Wardens, who hold back resources and dismiss her research as frivolous.","arc":"Juniper begins as a skeptic who trusts only measured charts. After Pip shows her a map that differs between yesterday and today, which the Wardens dismiss amid the Toll War