"Marigold Thrum","role":"supporting","description":"Pip's elderly grandmother, a retired master miller of The Hollow with silver braids, gnarled hands, and a laugh like creaking sails. She keeps old family secrets about the door that her late husband once built.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To pass on the mill and its quiet wisdom before her strength fails.","goal":"To keep the Hollow Circle united against the Cartel levy.","flaw":"Prideful; she hides her illness and refuses help.","internal_conflict":"She longs to tell Pip the truth about the door but fears burdening her with the family's past.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's levy threatens to leave the Circle's mills empty, and her failing health weakens her authority.","arc":"Marigold starts as a proud, secretive matriarch concealing her illness. After Pip's rift with her and the Cartel's early arrival at the mill, she is forced to admit her frailty before the Hollow Circle. She ends by sharing the door's history with Pip and handing over leadership of the mill, at peace with accepting help.","personality_traits":["proud","wise","dry-witted","secretive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Sense","description":"Can judge the quality and origin of any grain by scent alone.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Circle Authority","description":"Her word commands respect among Hollow farmers and millers.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_orrin_vale","name":"Orrin Vale","role":"antagonist","description":"A smooth-talking Drift Cartel levy agent from Mistral Docks, tall and sharp-featured, wearing a coat sewn with brass buttons stamped with the Cartel seal. He tallies grain and debts with equal relish.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To earn a promotion to the Cartel's inner council by collecting record levies.","goal":"To seize the Hollow's grain stores before the next wind-debt season closes.","flaw":"Greedy and dismissive of anyone he considers small or powerless.","internal_conflict":"He privately resents the Cartel's cruelty but suppresses that doubt to protect his ambition.","external_conflict":"The Hollow Circle resists the Grain Levy, and the strange events caused by Pip threaten his tallies and his reputation.","arc":"Orrin begins as a confident collector who sees the Hollow as a ledger line. When he is confused by Pip's repeated appearances in yesterday during the Grain Levy standoff, he discovers a child outwitting his schedule and is forced to confront the human cost of his tallies. He ends by quietly reporting a reduced levy, trading ambition for conscience.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","secretly conflicted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Mind","description":"Can recall every figure in a ledger after one reading.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Persuades and pressures with polished negotiation.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_juniper_quill","name":"Juniper Quill","role":"supporting","description":"A young cartographer-apprentice at Silverspine Academy with ink-stained fingers, round spectacles, and a habit of muttering coordinates. She charts skybridges and becomes intrigued by anomalies in yesterday's maps.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that the shifting skybridge network follows a hidden pattern.","goal":"To map the anomaly of the yesterday door and publish it at the Academy.","flaw":"Overly rigid; she distrusts anything that cannot be measured.","internal_conflict":"Her love of order clashes with her growing wonder at something that defies measurement.","external_conflict":"The Toll War strains the Wardens, who hold back resources and dismiss her research as frivolous.","arc":"Juniper begins as a skeptic who trusts only measured charts. After Pip shows her a map that differs between yesterday and today, which the Wardens dismiss amid the Toll War, she chooses to risk her standing by recording the anomaly as unexplained. She ends as a cartographer willing to leave blank spaces on a map.","personality_traits":["precise","skeptical","earnest","nervous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Can chart drifting bridge routes accurately from observation.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_brannock_ashe","name":"Brannock Ashe","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered Bridge Warden braider at Emberroost with soot-darkened forearms and a booming, kindly voice. He mends cloudstone cables and fears carelessness above all.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep every skybridge safe so no traveller falls.","goal":"To resist the Cartel's rising tolls without abandoning the bridges' upkeep.","flaw":"Stubborn and slow to trust outsiders, especially merchants.","internal_conflict":"He feels guilt over a past cable failure and fears he is no longer fit to guard others.","external_conflict":"The Toll War pits the Wardens against the Drift Cartel, and Cartel pressure squeezes his forge's supplies.","arc":"Brannock starts as a guilt-ridden, distrustful braider hiding in routine. When Pip, desperate to fix yesterday, carries a stray spark that nearly severs a bridge against the no-fire rule, he must decide whether to report her or trust her. He chooses to teach her bridge safety, easing his guilt and ending as a mentor who trusts again.","personality_traits":["gruff","protective","loyal","guilt-ridden"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Braids and repairs cloudstone cables with expert skill.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Spark Warden","description":"Can sense stray flame or sparks near a skybridge.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_pip_marigold_family","source_character_id":"chr_pip_wickerby","target_character_id":"chr_marigold_thrum","relationship_type":"family","description":"Pip Wickerby is the granddaughter of Marigold Thrum; their quarrel over yesterday drives Pip to use the door and strains their bond."},{"id":"rel_pip_orrin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_pip_wickerby","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_vale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Pip Wickerby repeatedly outmanoeuvres levy agent Orrin Vale through yesterday, amplifying the Grain Levy conflict between them."},{"id":"rel_orrin_marigold_rival","source_character_id":"chr_orrin_vale","target_character_id":"chr_marigold_thrum","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Orrin Vale pressures Marigold Thrum to surrender the Hollow's grain, while she rallies the Hollow Circle against his levy."},{"id":"rel_juniper_pip_ally","source_character_id":"chr_juniper_quill","target_character_id":"chr_pip_wickerby","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Juniper Quill studies Pip Wickerby's door and helps her chart yesterday, pushing Juniper against her rigid skepticism."},{"id":"rel_brannock_pip_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_brannock_ashe","target_character_id":"chr_pip_wickerby","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Brannock Ashe teaches Pip Wickerby skybridge safety after her stray spark endangers a bridge, testing his guilt and trust."},{"id":"rel_brannock_orrin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_brannock_ashe","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_vale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Brannock Ashe opposes Orrin Vale's Cartel tolls on the skybridges, fuelling the Toll War between Wardens and merchants."}]}
