{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_wren_ashcombe","name":"Wren Ashcombe","description":"A 19-year-old braider's apprentice at Emberroost, lean and soot-streaked, with burn-scarred fingers and a habit of humming while she works cable. Orphaned when her mother, a Bridge Warden, fell during a bridge failure, she keeps her mother's brass splicing needle on a cord at her neck. While salvaging cloudstone scrap, she discovers a warm, pulsing egg of unknown origin and hides it in a shielded forge-pit.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep alive the one living thing she has found since her mother's death, and prove that something can be saved rather than lost.","goal":"Hatch the egg and raise its occupant in secret until it is strong enough to leave the isles safely.","flaw":"Fiercely secretive; she shuts out every ally rather than risk being betrayed or having her find taken.","internal_conflict":"She wants someone to share her burden but believes that trusting anyone will cost her what she loves, as trust in a bridge once cost her mother.","external_conflict":"The egg's warmth must be kept in a shielded forge-pit, and open flame rules and Warden inspections make concealing it increasingly hard.","arc":"Starts as a guarded apprentice who hoards her secret alone. When the Warden inspection of the forge-pits nearly exposes the egg and Tobias covers for her, she is forced to see that isolation endangers it. She chooses to confide in him and Maren, ending as a young woman who accepts shared risk and entrusts the hatchling to a community.","personality_traits":["guarded","stubborn","tender","resourceful","grieving"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Skilled at braiding and splicing cloudstone cable, able to improvise shielded enclosures and cradles.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Quiet Stepping","description":"Moves unseen through forge corridors and bridge catwalks after years of dodging overseers.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_varn","name":"Tobias Varn","description":"A broad, soft-spoken Bridge Warden inspector in his fifties, with a grey braided beard and a limp from an old bridge collapse. He served alongside Wren's mother and has quietly watched over Wren since.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To atone for failing to save Wren's mother by protecting her daughter, whatever the cost to his career.","goal":"Keep Wren safe from the Toll War's reprisals while quietly learning what she is hiding.","flaw":"Chronic guilt that makes him overprotective and prone to lying to protect others.","internal_conflict":"He is sworn to report irregularities to the Wardens yet cannot bring himself to endanger Wren.","external_conflict":"Warden command demands full forge-pit inspections to counter Cartel sabotage during the Toll War.","arc":"Begins as a dutiful inspector who bends rules in silence. When ordered to inspect Wren's forge-pit, he finds the egg and chooses to falsify his report. By the end he stops hiding behind guilt, openly stands as Wren's ally, and accepts the loss of his post as a fair price.","personality_traits":["gentle","dutiful","guilt-ridden","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Structural Assessment","description":"Reads stress and fatigue in cables and stone at a glance.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_maren_quill","name":"Maren Quill","description":"A sharp-eyed cartographer in her thirties at Silverspine Academy, ink-stained and restless, who keeps annotated charts of old sky-migration routes that no longer match any living creature.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that the extinct wyrm routes in her charts reflect a real lost species, rescuing her discredited scholarship.","goal":"Find physical evidence of a surviving wyrm lineage and publish it before the Academy buries her work.","flaw":"Ambition that makes her treat living things as evidence rather than beings.","internal_conflict":"She longs for vindication but suspects publishing would doom what she discovers.","external_conflict":"The Academy ridicules her research and the wind-debt on her expeditions leaves her in debt to the Cartel.","arc":"Begins as a vindication-hungry scholar ready to trade secrets for credit. When Wren shows her the hatchling and the Cartel offers to clear her wind-debt for its location, she must pick between fame and the creature. She burns her notes, ending as its guardian rather than its chronicler.","personality_traits":["driven","brilliant","impatient","curious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts drift patterns and bridge routes, predicting safe crossings.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_cassian_dray","name":"Cassian Dray","description":"A silver-haired Drift Cartel factor at Mistral Docks, polished and courteous, with a signet ring of braided cloudstone. He treats every secret as a tradable commodity and is rising fast in the Cartel.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure a rare monopoly commodity that would cement his control over the Cartel's leadership.","goal":"Locate and seize the rumoured hatchling, then control access to it for profit.","flaw":"Possessiveness; he cannot tolerate anything valuable remaining outside his control.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears he is only a tool of the Cartel princes and craves a worth that is his own.","external_conflict":"The Toll War and Grain Levy strain Cartel finances, and rivals within the Cartel are ready to replace him if he fails.","arc":"Starts as a confident broker who sees the hatchling as property. When the Grain Levy backlash and Maren's burned notes leave him without proof, he tries to take it by force through wind-debt calls. His failure exposes his dependence on the princes, ending with him ruined or humbled, sharply aware that what he sought could never be owned.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","covetous","insecure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Uses wind-debt obligations to coerce others into labour, silence, or information.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_odalys_fenn","name":"Odalys Fenn","description":"A weathered miller in her sixties from The Hollow, with flour-dusted hands and a dry wit. She quietly shelters travellers and strays, and her windmills sit at the quiet edge of the isle.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect her community from the Cartel's grain levy and honour the self-reliance forged in the Great Calm.","goal":"Offer a hidden refuge on The Hollow for what Wren is hiding, while keeping her mills running.","flaw":"Stubborn pride; she refuses help and bears every burden alone, even when it endangers others.","internal_conflict":"She wants to shield the vulnerable but fears drawing Cartel wrath on her neighbours.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's levy on grain shipments threatens to ruin her mill and the Hollow Circle.","arc":"Begins as a proud miller who handles everything alone. When the levy collectors come and Wren arrives with the hatchling, she must accept the Circle's help to hide it. By the end she shares her refuge openly and learns that community strength outweighs solitary pride.","personality_traits":["dry-witted","proud","sheltering","resilient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Lore","description":"Understands wind patterns and can hide movement behind the churn of working mills.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_tobias_wren_guardian","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_varn","target_character_id":"chr_wren_ashcombe","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Tobias Varn watches over Wren Ashcombe out of guilt over her mother's death, and his protection puts him at odds with Warden orders."},{"id":"rel_wren_maren_uneasy_ally","source_character_id":"chr_wren_ashcombe","target_character_id":"chr_maren_quill","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Wren Ashcombe reluctantly confides in Maren Quill, whose scholarly hunger for the hatchling makes the alliance fragile."},{"id":"rel_cassian_wren_hunter","source_character_id":"chr_cassian_dray","target_character_id":"chr_wren_ashcombe","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Cassian Dray hunts for the hatchling Wren Ashcombe hides, using wind-debt and informants to close in on her."},{"id":"rel_cassian_maren_debt","source_character_id":"chr_cassian_dray","target_character_id":"chr_maren_quill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Cassian Dray holds Maren Quill's wind-debt over her to extract her research, forcing her to choose between fame and the creature."},{"id":"rel_odalys_wren_refuge","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_fenn","target_character_id":"chr_wren_ashcombe","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Odalys Fenn offers Wren Ashcombe a hidden refuge in The Hollow, risking Cartel retaliation over the grain levy."},{"id":"rel_cassian_odalys_levy","source_character_id":"chr_cassian_dray","target_character_id":"chr_odalys_fenn","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Cassian Dray enforces the Cartel's grain levy against Odalys Fenn, pressing her mill and her community."}]}
