ure exposes his dependence on the princes, ending with him ruined or humbled, sharply aware that what he sought could never be owned.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","covetous","insecure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Uses wind-debt obligations to coerce others into labour, silence, or information.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_odalys_fenn","name":"Odalys Fenn","description":"A weathered miller in her sixties from The Hollow, with flour-dusted hands and a dry wit. She quietly shelters travellers and strays, and her windmills sit at the quiet edge of the isle.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect her community from the Cartel's grain levy and honour the self-reliance forged in the Great Calm.","goal":"Offer a hidden refuge on The Hollow for what Wren is hiding, while keeping her mills running.","flaw":"Stubborn pride; she refuses help and bears every burden alone, even when it endangers others.","internal_conflict":"She wants to shield the vulnerable but fears drawing Cartel wrath on her neighbours.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's levy on grain shipments threatens to ruin her mill and the Hollow Circle.","arc":"Begins as a proud miller who handles everything alone. When the levy collectors come and Wren arrives with the hatchling, she must accept the Circle's help to hide it. By the end she shares her refuge openly and learns that community strength outweighs solitary pride.","personality_traits":["dry-witted","proud","sheltering","resilient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Lore","description":"Understands wind patterns and can hide movement behind the churn of working mills.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_tobias_wren_guardian","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_varn","target_character_id":"chr_wren_ashcombe","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Tobias Varn watches over Wren Ashcombe out of guilt over her mother's dea