ve","role":"supporting","description":"A broad, soft-spoken Bridge Warden of fifty-two with burn-scarred forearms from decades in Emberroost's forge-pits. He is the stern master engineer who first reviewed Isolde's work and now watches over her.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep every skybridge standing so no one repeats the loss he witnessed in his youth.","goal":"To keep the bridge network safe through proven engineering and to stop Isolde from taking untested risks with it.","flaw":"He mistrusts anything that cannot be measured or inspected.","internal_conflict":"He privately suspects the old methods are failing but cannot bear to admit the Wardens' craft is not enough.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's tolls strain the Wardens' budget, and Isolde's unexplained power threatens their authority.","arc":"Begins as a rigid gatekeeper who bans Isolde from the failing span. Watching the cable he braided heal under her voice, he lets her work alongside his crew. He ends as a mentor who accepts that craft and wonder can work together.","personality_traits":["disciplined","protective","gruff","fair"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"He braids cloudstone cable with a master's precision.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Stress Reading","description":"He can sense a cable's strain by touch.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_marisol_drake","name":"Marisol Drake","role":"antagonist","description":"A polished merchant princess of the Drift Cartel in her forties, with silver-threaded sails sewn into her coat and a patient smile. She runs the Mistral Docks shipping lanes and hears rumours of a girl who speaks to cloudstone.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's control over every crossing and protect the fortune her family built.","goal":"To bring Isolde under Cartel contract so that only the Cartel can repair, and charge for, the skybridges.","flaw":"She treats people as assets and cannot imagine loyalty that cannot be bought.","internal_conflict":"She is haunted by a fear of the Great Calm returning and leaving her family stranded and powerless, which she hides behind ambition.","external_conflict":"The Toll War and the Grain Levy have made the Wardens and the Hollow Circle her open enemies.","arc":"Starts as a confident schemer who tries to buy Isolde. When Isolde refuses her contract and heals a bridge for free, Marisol's levy-backed monopoly begins to crack. She ends by being forced to bargain openly or lose her influence.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","patient","ruthless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"She negotiates contracts that quietly favour her side.","category":"social"},{"name":"Lane Control","description":"She directs the Cartel's shipping lanes to pressure rivals.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_reed","name":"Tamsin Reed","role":"supporting","description":"A cheerful, sunburnt miller's daughter of twenty from The Hollow, with flour-dusted braids and a limp from a windmill accident. She became Isolde's closest friend while delivering grain to Silverspine.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect her community from the Cartel's grain levy and to look after the friend who believed in her.","goal":"To win allies against the Grain Levy and bring Isolde's power to the Hollow Circle's cause.","flaw":"She is fiercely loyal and impulsive, and she acts before thinking through the consequences.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between her duty to the Hollow and her wish to shield Isolde from being used by anyone, even her own people.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy is starving her family's mill of income, and she risks wind-debt she cannot repay.","arc":"Begins as an impulsive helper who tells the Hollow Circle about Isolde's gift in order to win support. When that leak lets Marisol's agents find Isolde, Tamsin owns the mistake and publicly argues for Isolde's right to choose her own path. She ends as a more careful but still loyal ally.","personality_traits":["warm","impulsive","loyal","talkative"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Lore","description":"She knows how to read the winds and keep grain mills running.","category":"other"},{"name":"Easy Rapport","description":"She quickly befriends strangers of any faction.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrove","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Corvin Ashgrove is Isolde Vane's reluctant mentor. He distrusts her unmeasurable gift and forbids her from the failing bridge, which sets up the tension between them."},{"id":"rel_marisol_isolde_pursuer","source_character_id":"chr_marisol_drake","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Marisol Drake pursues Isolde Vane to bind her to a Cartel contract, which would turn Isolde's gift into a tool for the Toll War."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_isolde_friend","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Tamsin Reed is Isolde Vane's closest friend. Her loyalty and her careless leak of Isolde's secret put Isolde in Marisol's path."},{"id":"rel_corvin_marisol_rival","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrove","target_character_id":"chr_marisol_drake","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Corvin Ashgrove and Marisol Drake are bitter rivals in the Toll War, which pits the Wardens' bridge upkeep against the Cartel's rising tolls."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_marisol_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_marisol_drake","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tamsin Reed opposes Marisol Drake because of the Cartel's Grain Levy on the Hollow Circle, which drives Tamsin to seek 